  "cause": [
    "Particle scale is never re-measured: walls, route-guide weights and resampling select short-stepping particles (undershoot survives dead ends/corners), so it drifted low within ~100 yards of every fix.",
    "scale_prior() re-seeded each new stretch from that surviving scale, weighted ~3:1 over the calibration (0.025 floor vs ~0.044 calibration sd), carrying the bias from stretch to stretch."
  ],
  "implemented": [
    "scale_prior() draws from the fix-to-fix calibration only.",
    "Each particle's log-scale reverts to the calibration over 250 walked yards with matching noise (stationary spread = calibration sd), batched per walked yard.",
    "The particles' weighted mean scale may not leave the calibration's 2-sd band (safety bound for sustained one-sided pressure; never triggered in these replays).",
    "Performance (bit-identical): key-only NCC sums cached per odometry key (surface 4.46 -> 2.92 ms/frame); cluster distance in _estimate computed per axis (3.46 -> 0.22 ms at 500 particles, 9.35 -> 1.24 ms at 4000)."
  ],
